Title: AudStories Showcase — The Call
Credit: AudStories Demo

EXT. STREET CORNER - MUMBAI - NIGHT

SFX: Heavy rain. Continuous, full, close.
Water running along a gutter nearby.
Distant traffic. City ambience underneath —
muffled, wet, indifferent.

A woman standing still inside all of it.

PRIYA
(V.O., quiet, to herself)
Twenty minutes.

Still nothing.

SFX: Rain. Traffic. Water in the gutter.

Her phone rings.

SFX: Phone ringtone — sharp, sudden,
cutting through rain.

A beat of silence where she doesn't
move.

Then —

SFX: Phone pickup. Click.

PRIYA
(careful, almost afraid to speak)
Hello.

SFX: Phone crackle. Distant line quality.
Rain continues underneath.

VIKRAM
(through phone filter, quiet, measured)
Is this Priya Menon.

PRIYA
(still)
Yes.

VIKRAM
(through filter)
My name is Vikram.

You don't know me.

SFX: Rain fills the silence.
Water running. City breathing.

VIKRAM (CONT'D)
(through filter, carefully)
But I knew your brother.

SFX: The city ambience pulls back
slightly — almost imperceptibly.
Rain remains. Everything else
recedes.

Priya says nothing.

Five full seconds.

Only rain.

PRIYA
(barely a whisper)
My brother has been missing
for two years.

VIKRAM
(through filter)
I know.

I know where he is.

SFX: A single musical note —
low, sparse, one bowed string.
Enters beneath the rain.
Underneath everything.

PRIYA
(voice breaking, just slightly)
Where.

VIKRAM
(through filter, after a long beat)
That's why I'm calling.

(silence)

He asked me to.

SFX: Rain continues.
The music holds — unresolved,
patient.

SFX: Music fades slowly into rain.
Rain fades slowly into silence.

FADE TO SILENCE.

SFX: Silence. Three full seconds.

NEUTRAL VOICE
(clean, unhurried)
Your story deserves to be heard.
Not just read.
AudStories.

FADE OUT.